### Other

4 of 71 posts.

Four posts have other main concerns: repairing an inaccessible toy battery compartment while a child cries; assessing whether fostering dogs is safe around a two-year-old still grabbing kittens; an acquaintance's second-hand attempt to help a sleepless one-year-old and their mother; and a two-year-old's rock-in-the-nose incident. The repair post's child's age is unknown, and the acquaintance's account does not establish the child's mother's own wording. These are retained separately rather than treated as first-hand reports of one shared behaviour.

- "I should of just thrown the whole thing in the trash. Now I am sitting on the kitchen floor trying to drill out a two millimeter screw while my kid screams. The screw is just COMPLETELY destroyed. Why is this even a thing." [sr081-0090]
- "My children are 2, 4, and 6. The 2 yo in particular is still very much learning to respect animals boundaries. We have two fairly new kittens and I am constantly having to rescue them from her clutches. I feel like I would have to be so insanely picky that I would hardly be useful as a foster resource for them." [sr089-0080]
- "I'm talking to a girl who's having trouble with her 1-year-old son. I like her and want to help and take care of her." [sr095-0099]
- "What could possibly possess them to think it lol. No worries we got it out after a quick blow (and about 30min of me dry heaving) and no tears were shed until I threw her snot treasure in the trash." [sr131-0022]

