### Other

4 of 72 posts.

One post concerns an age-unknown child scattering objects during play, and another a recently two-year-old spitting water into toys and containers. A parent of a fourteen-month-old reports hysterical crying at a new septum piercing and postpones trying it again. The fourth parent seeks help for a twenty-three-month-old's persistent congestion and disturbed sleep, alongside poor weight gain and daytime frustration, after several medical opinions and treatments. These are distinct situations rather than one shared behavioural explanation.

- "It’s hilarious but also drives me mad 😂😂😂" [sr025-0063]
- "she’s figured out that she can hold her water in her mouth and spit it in different containers, she also tries to spit in her dinosaurs mouths and her toys." [sr077-0110]
