## Pattern 3, share 08: across the yes posts

| Tag | Posts |
|---|---|
| tried | 176 of 210 |
| others | 84 of 210 |
| bought | 4 of 210 |
| feeling | 132 of 210 |

Each post has one primary form and four yes/no tags. Here, tried means a stated action or attempt, including seeking advice; others means reported advice, judgments, help or distinct responses by other people, including a partner or other children. Feeling means the speaker expresses an emotion, fatigue or distress, rather than only describing the child’s feelings. A no means it was not stated, not that it did not happen. Counts describe the posts assigned to this share of pattern 3 within the random sample; they are not counts of people or estimates of market prevalence.

### What they tried, in their words

- "nothing worked until we caved and gave her a pacifier. she immediately stopped her tantrum once she got the pacifier." [sr004-0031]
- "I’ve tried with children’s toothpaste, without toothpaste , I’ve tried sitting her in the sink so she can see herself, doing it at the same time with her, letting her do it first, then me." [sr003-0166]
- "We did time out/safe space for hitting and it worked to make him stop and think before he did it, then he started calculating it was worth it and doing it anyway." [sr021-0025]
- "No matter how many times we try to tell her (including high voice and hitting hands), she just doesn't care, and keeps doing it!" [sr067-0060]
- "We’re working on it, and using sign language has helped tremendously." [sr046-0124]
- "Anyways, I have now resorted to changing his diapers -even poop diapers- with him standing. I put something distracting on tv and he stands up holding his playpen or something like a chair/ottoman." [sr059-0062]
- "We’ve tried it all. Reflux meds? Got em. Tongue tie? Procedure booked. Chiro, lactation consultant, osteopath? Seen them all." [sr044-0085]
- "i tried putting an empty bowl on his table, and that helped, he would put the rest of his peice in there sometimes." [sr114-0058]
- "Regular stops, happy song, toys, singing, even resorted to some screen time for cartoons but no joy." [sr099-0155]
- "I took a big step and booked an appointment with a therapist for anger issues, depression and anxiety, but I still don't feel its enough." [sr030-0022]
- "when he is breastfeeding i instantly say “no” in a gentle but firm voice and we’re immediately done," [sr118-0085]
- "When your child asks a question wanting something, literally anything, take a pause and think about your answer and then follow through. Every. Single. Time." [sr076-0069]

### What other people told them or did

- "when I asked my dad he said "bite her back," which is insane" [sr022-0002]
- "My husbands b!tchy step mom said my son is bad and that I’m not strict enough parenting him." [sr053-0164]
- "everyone kept telling me to put him down drowsy but awake (never worked)." [sr002-0086]
- "His pediatrician told me we had to wait until 5 ear infections for him to be referred to the pediatric ENT for tubes" [sr030-0075]
- "Our pediatrician recommended that we completely ignore the throwing and say nothing." [sr125-0035]
- "From conversations with his teachers, the biting seems to happen mostly during disputes over toys or other items in the classroom. Other times, it appears to be related to personal space issues." [sr042-0075]
- "Before bed, my wife sat him down and had a 1 on 1 talk with him trying to explain what he did was wrong, but also how even though he was wrong for his actions, it didn't justify my actions either, which I totally agree with." [sr030-0021]
- "My husband thinks that after she hits or throws something, we should walk away for 2–3 minutes into a different room and leave her to figure it out on her own." [sr066-0105]
- "My parents said they have never seen something like it. Today I told my sister in law about how I change his diaper and she was in shock." [sr059-0063]
- "Someone offered to give him a juice box so I thought that was nice." [sr005-0087]
- "They added an extra teacher to watch him but but he still managed to bite 3 kids in less than a hour." [sr028-0024]
- "She said this is all age appropriate behavior and she has been sometimes giving my daughter space to play on her own or give her alone time with certain toys while the babies are doing a different activity." [sr088-0120]

### What they bought or paid for

Only four yes posts clearly describe a completed purchase, a food order or money spent. The five excerpts below include the cruise and its disappointing value from the same post. Merely owning or trying an item, care without a stated payment, possible future purchases and a house purchase still in progress are not counted. The $14 produce claim comes from the humorous rant, recorded as stated.

- "I bought reusable waterproof covers to put over his diaper at night thinking 1) it may make it a little more difficult to move the diaper and 2) it might catch the pee so that it doesn’t soak his clothes/sheets, but we tried them and he is still managing to pee out of that." [sr071-0058]
- "I order her mashed potatoes to eat when we go to lunch" [sr080-0142]
- "Today is the last day of a 7 day Caribbean cruise." [sr091-0060]
- "after spending all this money and taking a full week off work I’m feeling so defeated and upset after this vacation instead of being sad that it’s over." [sr091-0065]
- "And apparently what he REALLY wanted was to finger-paint the high chair with sweet potatoes and feed the dogs $14 worth of organic produce." [sr133-0129]

### How they say they feel

- "The resentment is building up and I feel so bad about it. I’m at a point I don’t even want the baby I’m due to have in a month because I can’t handle anymore crying." [sr030-0070]
- "Sometimes after trying everything to calm him, I’ll just set him down mid-scream, stare at him, and question if we ruined our lives. And I hate myself for even thinking that." [sr044-0084]
- "if you told me this is the life i would’ve been living then i honestly don’t think i would’ve wanted to have children." [sr072-0076]
- "My mom recently passed away unexpectedly and very tragic, and while I’m grieving my mom it’s so hard to be present with my baby" [sr015-0074]
- "But juggling an 8,7 and 2 year old with a baby I can't put down has me wanting to stick my head in the meat grinder by the end of the day." [sr005-0160]
- "I'm so lonely, I have no mom friends and no one to turn to." [sr017-0238]
- "I just feel like a shit parent and I just hate myself for not taking it all in my stride." [sr116-0054]
- "I am a swallower and a retreater. And my 1.5yo has me swallowing my frustration and wanting to retreat somewhere alone just like all day." [sr112-0012]
- "I feel like a ball of nerves from the second I wake up because I don’t know what mood he’s going to be in that day." [sr127-0064]
- "I feel so sad that I’ve not been able to enjoy this time with her as a baby like everyone else around me seems to be doing." [sr003-0134]
- "I didn’t want advice sorry, just wanted to hear others who have had crappy days so I don’t have to feel so alone" [sr077-0057]
- "I can love this child with every molecule of my existence and still fantasize about checking into a hotel alone for 24 hours, ordering room service, and taking a shit with the door CLOSED." [sr133-0137]

