Parents of children aged eight to 23 months describe clamped mouths, blocked teeth, toothpaste sucking and screaming when an adult brushes. Games, modelling, taking turns and an electric toothbrush have not consistently worked. Parents weigh clean teeth and avoiding cavities against force, upsetting the child and fear of creating a lasting aversion.

- "The only way to do it properly is to pin him down and do it myself." [sr022-0029]
