- "Thanks! We got an electric toothbrush. Maybe I’ll let her just play with it for a while, because she won’t put it in her mouth yet. What toothpaste did you get that he liked?" [sr002-0063]

**But:** Resistance can replace earlier enjoyment rather than reflect an unchanged dislike: "The first couple of times he actually liked it and let us brush them, but now we have to hold him down and he blocks his teeth with his tongue which is freakishly strong." [sr036-0042]

