Parents of children from seven months to nearly two describe newly intense protests at limits, waiting, transitions or requests they cannot satisfy. Some report head-banging, sweating, breath-holding or hyperventilation, and struggle to distinguish ordinary frustration from unusually severe episodes. They ask about calming, boundaries and whether the phase will pass; a few use humour or report a change that helped.

- "She gets so worked up she sweats and is almost hyperventilating. Sometimes she hits her own head on the floor too and all I can do is put my hands between her head and the floor as if I pick her up I'll get hit!" [sr067-0041]
