## Pattern 3, share 09: across the yes posts

Counts describe supplied post records within this pattern share of the tagged 20,000-post random sample, not people or the market. Each post has one main form even when it contains several situations. Posts 1v911kd and 1v91ajo reproduce the same wording and remain two records as supplied. Tags are independent: tried requires a stated action or approach already used for the situation; others includes explicitly reported advice, caregiving, reactions, peer actions and comparisons with other children; collective “we” alone is not a report about another person; bought requires explicit buying, paying or ordering a named item or service; feeling records expressed adult emotion or overwhelm, rather than the child's feelings alone. Possessions, gifts, proposed purchases and an unspecified Amazon-basket item do not establish buying. All share records were read; no post was excluded. Ages and identities are retained as reported, including unknown values. A hidden per-post ledger below preserves all four yes/no tags for both sections. Near post 1weh91t reports an inconsistent chronological/adjusted age; that discrepancy is left unresolved.

| Tag | Posts |
|---|---|
| tried | 194 of 210 |
| others | 117 of 210 |
| bought | 6 of 210 |
| feeling | 153 of 210 |

### What they tried, in their words

- "We’ve tried baths (but he’s not a huge fan), bouncing, walking around the room, fresh air (but we can’t do a full walk due to our older child going to bed at this time and our neighborhood being a little sketchy at night), bicycle kicks/massages, rocking, singing." [sr016-0085]
- "Was LO on a different formula before or breastmilk? I EBF and tried cutting dairy and soy from my diet for a month, but it didn’t help much." [sr021-0002]
- "But it’s been several months now and is only escalating to now hitting me and dad as well. I’ve tried immediately separating them, showering sister in positive attention while ignoring him, time out, gentle hands, ignoring it, acting sad, complete redirection to a toy or hitting a pillow, pretty much every option presented and he goes along with it and will immediately turn around and do it again. And often laugh." [sr028-0004]
- "At the moment I offer a hug or physical contact, then validate, then explain why she cant have it, and tell her what she/we will do instead and she calms." [sr085-0094]
- "At the moment, we're pinning him down to get it done, but I hate having to do that. We're trying to offer cuddles in between and give him a countdown but it's not helping, my husband offered the screen his morn which helped but I don't want this to be the long-term solution" [sr082-0071]
- "I didn't raise my voice or give up, just up correcting the behavior until I got it done." [sr002-0103]
- "I lost my mind. Knowing that I would have to give him a shower while in tight schedule for work, I lost it and slapped his hand. He started crying but looked at my dead in the eyes and did again, this time hand full on the poop and he smeared it everywhere on himself and on the changing station." [sr129-0036]
- "There are days I got frustrated and smacked her butt. But I sit with myself at the end of the night and reflect that I do not want to be that kind of mother, be like my mother. I want my daughter to be able to regulate her emotions in a safe environment." [sr053-0171]
- "We talked to her pediatrician about it and she said it's normal. We've checked for diaper rashes, UTI's, etc. and everything is fine with baby girl." [sr051-0022]
- "\- bribing with snacks […] \- bringing favourite toys […] \- trying to wait out the resistance by letting her stand in the stroller for a while and hoping she eventually sits down […] \- distracting with kid songs from youtube" [sr074-0063]

### What other people told them or did

- "He then tells me “why don’t you spank her” I told him that I’m trying my best to NOT do that. He says “we’re not white people to be doing that stuff”." [sr053-0170]
- "Thank you I will look into her! It’s just very frustrating having other parents in your ear saying “oh my kids know better” or “we don’t let that slide” like I don’t either but he keeps doing it😭" [sr030-0148]
- "I live in UAE and it's so common for parents to not have car seats... Even though it's illegal. Also many parents use the car seats as storage but keep the baby in their laps. There are so many daily deadly car accidents here and I constantly get made fun of or scolded for letting my baby cry because I want to keep her in the car seat for safety. People here drive around 120 to 140 km/hr and the drivers are extremely reckless. It usually takes us 20 to 30 minutes to reach a destination." [sr048-0007]
- "The daycare just keeps assuring us they are doing their best and keeping a close watch to try and intervene when this is happening. I am fairly certain it is the same child who is consistently biting her as one of the teachers told me that." [sr110-0054]
- "My nanny even told me she’s one of the most emotionally regulated toddlers she’s ever seen." [sr127-0123]
- "I’m glad to hear from other parents that stepping in gently but firmly is appreciated (“soft hands”, please be gentle” as I do with my daughter). I was just shocked in the moment and as a FTM I didn’t know what would be appropriate except physically separate them." [sr013-0009]
- "Today, our son’s lead teacher at daycare informed me that they’re working with him on not taking toys from other children. She said he is generally a pleasant and sweet boy, but if he sees a toy he wants to play with, he’ll cry if he can’t have it and even try to take it from another child." [sr074-0138]
- "My in laws have offered to help in whatever way they can, but my husband doesn’t want to use them due to their lack of consistent availability and I’m not sure how to best use them." [sr020-0105]
- "Our daycare has been wonderful throughout all of this. They catch incidents as much as they can, communicate with us, and have been very supportive. They’re not threatening expulsion or anything like that. I know it’s developmentally common, but I want to help it be smoother at daycare." [sr044-0097]
- "Again a clear over reaction to words. There were more comments who assured that this is a phase and the baby will pass it and other who advised few tips that calmed me down and will give me more strengh. I hoped that you could at least do the right thing in a moment of frustration." [sr001-0111]

### What they bought or paid for

- "I bring him to the park, I pay to go to indoor play places, I take him to grocery shopping with me and try to get him involved but he just cries." [sr016-0123]
- "\- buying new stroller" [sr074-0062]
- "I bought one of those visors to keep the water out of his eyes. Haven’t used it yet. But decided to stop wetting/washing his hair to at least diminish the association." [sr052-0027]
- "We’re going to start potty training this weekend. That’s a whole other thing. I know we need to, but have no clue how. I’ve bought training undies and a potty. But I’m not prepared." [sr088-0124]
- "We bought a book called "teeth are not for biting" but he refuses to read that one book in particular. We asked the daycare to offer him teether, we brought teether and his stuffy from home." [sr133-0026]
- "I was heating up the kids meal we had ordered him the night prior- grilled chicken tenders and sweet potato. The meal had a ramekin of honey mustard sauce and I also took out a quarter loaf of bread." [sr112-0018]

### How they say they feel

- "I think what’s hardest is the nonstop nature of it. The crying, impatience, moods, constant touching, constant movement, constant needing me. I don’t feel like a person anymore sometimes." [sr029-0026]
- "I absolutely understand that but it brings instant tears to think I have to PRACTICE liking my child. That’s not how it’s supposed to be." [sr038-0139]
- "i’m just honestly so frustrated & i cry every day because i miss my old life. i feel like im just a fat mom now. i love my son & i was really excited for this pregnancy but i feel like im barely holding on to my sanity with one kid & i don’t know how im going to make it with another one on the way. i feel guilty because my babies didn’t ask to be here & i want to be the best version of myself for them but it’s just so hard, honestly." [sr055-0090]
- "I obviously know it’s one of those baby things and I don’t take it sexually, but I feel like my nervous system does. I get so touched out and triggered that I feel rage building inside me as if I’m being physically/ sexually attacked and’s need to protect myself. I feel like I’ve acquired psychological damage from suppressing my fight or flight, suffering through inflicted pain and inappropriate touching just to keep from being hit and screamed at. And how guilty I sometimes feel for not wanting to be touched at all by him despite all of that." [sr090-0042]
- "I feel ashamed of myself, I am so against physical violence. I felt so trapped and didn’t know better at that moment. I know there something I am doing wrong (besides the obvious hand slapping), I am missing something." [sr129-0037]
- "I struggled to get pregnant so I feel incredibly guilty to admit that I don’t love being a mom. My son has always been very clingy but even more so now that he’s 18 months. It’s to an extreme level! I can’t get up to grab water, can’t use the bathroom, can’t put him down for a second without him crying." [sr105-0069]
- "My baby will be 4 weeks tomorrow. Over the last couple of days he has become inconsolable. He cries for hours and is only happy if he is being fed or help upright. He has been refusing naps. He has barely napped over the last two days. Idk what to do anymore and have spent the majority of the day crying. I have the urge to get in the car and never come back." [sr091-0077]
- "I was just so embarrassed. I started tearing up and kept my head down. I know everyone around me was staring and judging. I got into my car and just broke down. I guess I know how she feels when emotions just run over lol 🤷‍♀️. Why is it so incredibly embarrassing and stressful when your toddler acts up in public?" [sr127-0016]
- "He doesn’t hurt me because he’s angry, he just can’t be gentle yet. When I pick him up he pinches me every single time. I’m covered in bruises. I didn’t know before having him that you could get a child who hurts you constantly. Like really really hurts you. My body is just exhausted. Being constantly hurt has messed me up so bad. I’m always on edge waiting for pain." [sr079-0023]
- "I am feeling so low, and I’m not enjoying being a mother." [sr014-0065]

