## Pattern 3, share 08: yes posts

### They want to stop their child hurting them or someone else, including during play.

35 of 210 posts.

These posts describe hitting, biting, scratching, pinching, hair pulling and head-butting from about five months to almost two years; targets include parents, siblings, peers and pets. Some incidents follow frustration or correction, while others happen during excitement, affection, nursing or falling asleep. Parents report injuries, repeated unsuccessful correction and daycare suspensions or exclusions; one speaker is an aunt rather than a parent.

- "I’m a SAHM so I take the brunt of his abuse and I’m at my limit." [sr069-0097]
- "My 21 month old keeps bitting kids at daycare and its not out of anger or anything he just goes up and bites them. Hes been suspended 2 time which I understand but I just need advice." [sr028-0022]
- "He truly just will see someone doing something and for example, pull their pigtails and pull them to the ground." [sr021-0046]
- "He seems to be pinching in a self-soothing manner." [sr060-0002]
- "But she does it when she’s done eating or at least close to being done, so she really doesn’t care when I unlatch and set her down when she bites." [sr130-0028]
- "I am hoping to discourage the behavior without doing anything weird or traumatizing (when I asked my dad he said "bite her back," which is insane)." [sr022-0002]

**But:** Some parents report improvement alongside the injuries; these posts do not all describe deliberate anger or escalation. "Yes. It got better. I mean still basic sibling nonsense still. And hitting still comes up but not as bad." [sr001-0071]

