main='''# baby-development: pattern 3, Hard behaviour

**Written:** 2026-11-20 from baby-development/evidence/2026-11/second-reading/digest-08.md baby-development/evidence/2026-11/second-reading/digest-09.md
**Reviewed by the owner:** not yet

## Limits

A keyword-free random sample of 20,000 Reddit posts from twelve parenting subreddits, 1 April–24 October 2026, yielded 2,471 on-niche posts; this pattern has 420 on-niche and 143 near posts. Counts record posts tagged by one reader; forms were merged across digest readers by judgement, and these are not people or market prevalence. Both digests were read whole; two supplied records repeat wording, unknown ages remain unknown, one near-post age is inconsistent, and cross-tags overlap; absent tags mean unstated.
'''
def render(claim,n,total,body,qs,but):
    return '\\n### '+claim+'\\n\\n'+f'{n} of {total} posts.\\n\\n'+body+'\\n\\n'+'\\n'.join('- '+s for s in qs)+'\\n\\n**But:** '+but+'\\n'
for sec,title,total in [('yes','On-niche posts',420),('near','Near posts',143)]:
    main+='\\n## '+title+'\\n'
    for _,claim,n,body,qs,but in sorted([f for f in F if f[0]==sec],key=lambda f:(f[1].startswith('Other'),-f[2])):
        main+=render(claim,n,total,body,qs,but)
main+='\\n## Across the on-niche posts\\n'
for claim,n,body,qs,but in cross:main+=render(claim,n,420,body,[q(*x) for x in qs],but)
print('Above Coverage:',len(main.split()),'words;',len(F),'form findings')
cov='''\\n## Coverage

<details>
<summary>Every heading of the digests, and where it went</summary>

| Digest heading | Went to |
|---|---|
'''
for h,k in headings:cov+='| '+h+' | '+(mapping[k] if k else 'section title')+' |\\n'
cov+='\\n</details>\\n'
assert len(main.split())<=2500,len(main.split())
Path('baby-development/findings/2026-11/patterns/pattern-03.md').write_text(main+cov)
